= Turing machine — Simple =

A '''Turing machine''' is a very simple imaginary computer used to study what computation can and cannot do.

It has a tape made of cells, a head that can read and write one cell, and rules telling it what to do next.

The tape is treated as unlimited in the mathematical model.

Even though the machine is simple, it can represent any algorithm that can be expressed in the standard models of general computation.

A universal Turing machine can simulate other Turing machines.

Turing machines also show limits: some problems, such as the halting problem, cannot be solved by any general algorithm.

